2026-08-26] NVIDIA guided Q3 FY2027 revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, with no Data Center compute revenue from China assumed.\nP/user.txt:32:    Quote: Revenue is expected to be $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%. NVIDIA is not assuming any Data Center compute revenue from China in its outlook.\nP/user.txt:52:    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e2721, e3213, e3405, e3589; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\nP/user.txt:115:- e4896 [fact; Zacks.com; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:13952dff579190ce77353acd 2026-09-14] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $96.2 billion in FY2027 Q2, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially.\nP/user.txt:116:    Quote: NVIDIA's revenues reached $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, representing a 106% year-over-year increase and an 18% rise sequentially, according to the company's Aug. 26 press release.\nP/user.txt:149:- e4925 [fact; fxleaders.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:4dca50e22bd9f158d2a04186 2026-09-14] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 100% year over year.\nP/user.txt:150:    Quote: Revenue for fiscal Q2 stood at $96.2 billion, twice as much as the previous year\nP/user.txt:162:- e4962 [fact; Stephen Guilfoyle; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2fc71ee9730f9420d6d130bd 2026-09-14] NVIDIA reported fiscal second-quarter adjusted EPS of $2.22 and revenue of $96.22 billion, with revenue up 106% year over year and more than $4.0 billion above Wall Street expectations.\nP/user.txt:163:    Quote: Again. Just three weeks ago, Nvidia reported its fiscal second-quarter financial results. The company posted adjusted EPS of $2.22 on revenue of $96.22 billion. That beat Wall Street by more than $4.0 billion and was good for year-over-year growth of 106%.\nP/user.txt:165:- e4963 [party_statement; Stephen Guilfoyle; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:2fc71ee9730f9420d6d130bd 2026-09-14] NVIDIA projected current-quarter revenue of $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%, versus consensus of $104.6 billion; the projection implied roughly 90% year-over-year growth.\nP/user.txt:166:    Quote: For the current quarter, CEO Jensen Huang’s firm projected revenue of $108.0 billion (+/-2%) vs. consensus for $104.6 billion. That would be good for growth of roughly 90% and Nvidia Is known for beating its guidance.\nP/user.txt:186:- e4983 [fact; Zacks.com analyst; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:1d3bc1ba4c2df5e998884bdb 2026-09-14] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q2 2027 revenue of $96.22 billion, up 106% year over year.\nP/user.txt:187:    Quote: In the second quarter of fiscal 2027, revenues surged 106% year over year to $96.22 billion\nP/user.txt:204:- e5002 [fact; Zacks analyst; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from gnews:955c64e5a5907651550e94b8 2026-09-15] NVIDIA reported fiscal Q2 2027 total revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% quarter over quarter.\nP/user.txt:205:    Quote: the company's fiscal second-quarter 2027 revenues reached $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year and 18% quarter over quarter.\nP/user.txt:230:- e5021 [fact; fool.com (analyst); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:6261d9e9a1fe8d22c05f5e82 2026-09-15] NVIDIA reported FY2027 Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, net income of $59.7 billion, up 126%, and capital spending of $2.7 billion.\nP/user.txt:231:    Quote: Revenue grew 106% year over year to $96.2 billion in the quarter, and net income climbed 126% to $59.7 billion -- yet capital spending was just $2.7 billion.\nP/user.txt:249:- e5047 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5adb2372d28f9339f479435d 2026-09-15] NVIDIA reported fiscal 2027 second-quarter total revenue of $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, and Data Center revenue of $89 billion, up 117%.\nP/user.txt:250:    Quote: Nvidia generated $96.2 billion of revenue in its fiscal 2027 second quarter, up 106% year-over-year (YoY), while data center revenue reached $89 billion, up 117%.\nP/user.txt:300:- e5078 [fact; finance.yahoo.com author; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:3f21db1f9791e20f80909da8 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 total revenue of $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year.\nP/user.txt:301:    Quote: Q2 FY2027 revenue landed at $96.22 billion, up 105.8% year over year\nP/user.txt:303:- e5081 [party_statement; finance.yahoo.com author; original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:3f21db1f9791e20f80909da8 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management guided Q3 FY2027 total revenue to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%.\nP/user.txt:304:    Quote: Management then guided Q3 to $108.0 billion, plus or minus 2%\nP/user.txt:309:- e5089 [fact; barchart.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:5c5a96c670714dee86769d87 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported revenue of $96.2 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, up 106% year over year.\nP/user.txt:310:    Quote: Further, in the second quarter, its top line hit $96.2 billion. That was a 106% increase YoY.\nP/user.txt:328:    Quote: During the fiscal second quarter of 2027 (the period ended July 26), $27.0 billion of Nvidia's revenue was billed to customers headquartered in Taiwan. That's 28% of the quarter's $96.2 billion total.\nP/user.txt:337:- e5105 [fact; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA reported total revenue of $96.2 billion in fiscal Q2 2027, up 106% year over year, with about 92% from Data Center.\nP/user.txt:338:    Quote: Companywide revenue totaled $96.2 billion, up 106% year over year, and about 92% of it came from the data center business.\nP/user.txt:345:- e5108 [party_statement; fool.com (author); original source NVIDIA management ; from gnews:147e79a4a1f10279da449944 2026-09-16] NVIDIA management forecast total revenue of $108.0 billion for fiscal Q3 2027.\nP/user.txt:346:    Quote: Management's forecast for the fiscal third quarter, now underway, is $108.0 billion of revenue -- and growth like that is ultimately a claim about what 