quentially.\nP/user.txt:577:    Quote: According to NVIDIA’s Aug. 26 press release, the company’s total revenues reached $96.2 billion in the fiscal second quarter of 2027, up 106% year over year and 18% sequentially.\nP/user.txt:607:- e2721 [party_statement; Colette Kress; original source NVIDIA 2026-08-26; from truenorth:transcript:NVDA:2026-08-26 2026-08-26] NVIDIA expects Vera Rubin to account for about 20% of Data Center revenue in Q3 FY2027.\nP/user.txt:616:- e3401 [third_party_view; fool.com (Daniel Sparks); original source Daniel Sparks 2026-08-28; from gnews:387b486b6e29491b9c8506df 2026-08-28] Daniel Sparks calculated that Data Center revenue would be $99.9 billion in fiscal Q3 2027 if NVIDIA total revenue reaches its $108.0 billion guidance midpoint and Data Center remains 92.5% of the mix.\nP/user.txt:639:- e4907 [fact; finance.yahoo.com; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:7708a5ba7485f4ee381ccc41 2026-09-14] NVIDIA reported Data Center revenue of $83.7 billion out of $96.22 billion in total revenue for the second quarter.\nP/user.txt:640:    Quote: the data center business accounting for $83.7 billion out of the $96.22 billion of the total revenue.\nP-v4/user.txt:17:- e1041 [fact; 247wallst.com (Alex Sirois); original source Meta ; from gnews:4f1770366917aea8eed6ae4c 2026-07-24] Meta signed for a deployment of up to 6 GW of AMD Instinct GPUs, a competing accelerator commitment relevant to NVIDIA's FY2027 revenue outlook.\nP-v4/user.txt:25:- e2649 [fact; NVIDIA Corporation; original source NVIDIA Corporation 2026-08-26; from nvidianews:nvidia-announces-financial-results-for-second-quarter-fiscal-2027 2026-08-26] NVIDIA reported Q2 FY2027 revenue of $96.2 billion, up 18% quarter over quarter and 106% year over year.\nP-v4/user.txt:26:    Quote: NVIDIA (NASDAQ: NVDA) today reported revenue for the second quarter ended July 26, 2026, of $96.2 billion, up 18% from the previous quarter and up 106% from a year ago.\nP-v4/user.txt:28:- e2652 [party_statement; 