Bram Berkowitz, fool.com, reporting Colette Kress's statement; original source NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress ; from gnews:fd25a8ea6f60290264bfbe55 2026-08-30] NVIDIA CFO Colette Kress said NVIDIA still expects $20 billion of CPU revenue in FY2027 and expects FY2028 CPU revenue to more than double that amount.\nO/user.txt\n[Family] members:\nThesis v29 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA's committed equity investments in ecosystem partners\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much will NVIDIA's equity investment commitments reach at the publication of its FY2027 annual report?\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: Commitments are below $25 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: Commitments are at least $25 billion and below $50 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: Commitments are at least $50 billion and below $75 billion. / rung 4 Bearish: Commitments are at least $75 billion and below $100 billion. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: Commitments are at least $100 billion.\n\nRelations: none.\nShared quantities, one forecast figure each, through which every figure an outcome uses for that quantity goes: none.\nOutcome keys (population | measure | scope | period), in USD bn, to be used exactly: v29 = NVIDIA | equity investment commitments | company | end of FY2027 (the balance at the end of FY2027, as the FY2027 annual report publishes it).\n\n[Evidence in view for the family, 30 items]\n- e1732 [third_party_view; finance.yahoo.com; original source Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya ; from gnews:d024d71d75661d369798d307 2026-08-12] Bank of America analyst Vivek Arya said NVIDIA had committed to provide $70 billion in equity investments to ecosystem partners; the period covered was not specified.\nP-v4/user.txt\n[Family] members:\nThesis v4 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA total revenue in FY2027\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: Total revenue is at least $431.2 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: Total revenue is at least $392 billion and below $431.2 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: Total revenue is at least $352.8 billion and below $392 billion. / rung 4 Bearish: Total revenue is at least $313.6 billion and below $352.8 billion. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: Total revenue is below $313.6 billion.\n\nRelations: none.\nScopes: NVIDIA revenue Data Center is part of NVIDIA revenue company. A sum never adds the part into the whole for the same period; a difference may take the part from the whole of the same period only to give the rest.\nShared quantities, one forecast figure each, through which every figure an outcome uses for that quantity goes: NVIDIA, revenue, company, FY2027 Q3; NVIDIA, revenue, company, FY2027 Q4.\nOutcome keys (population | measure | scope | period), in USD bn, to be used exactly: v4 = NVIDIA | revenue | company | FY2027.\n\n[Evidence in view for the family, 296 items]\nP-v8/user.txt\n[Family] members:\nThesis v8 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA Data Center segment revenue in FY2027\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $400 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $350 billion and less than $400 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $300 billion and less than $350 billion. / rung 4 Bearish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $250 billion and less than $300 billion. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is les\n\nRelations: none.\nScopes: NVIDIA revenue Data Center is part of NVIDIA revenue company. A sum never adds the part into the whole for the same period; a difference may take the part from the whole of the same period only to give the rest.\nShared quantities, one forecast figure each, through which every figure an outcome uses for that quantity goes: NVIDIA, revenue, company, FY2027 Q3; NVIDIA, revenue, company, FY2027 Q4.\nOutcome keys (population | measure | scope | period), in USD bn, to be used exactly: v8 = NVIDIA | revenue | Data Center | FY2027.\n\n[Evidence in view for the family, 296 items]\nP/user.txt\n[Family] members:\nThesis v4 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA total revenue in FY2027\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: Total revenue is at least $431.2 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: Total revenue is at least $392 billion and below $431.2 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: Total revenue is at least $352.8 billion and below $392 billion. / rung 4 Bearish: Total revenue is at least $313.6 billion and below $352.8 billion. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: Total revenue is below $313.6 billion.\n\nThesis v8 (NVDA, asset, focus \"NVIDIA Data Center segment revenue in FY2027\", FY2027, due 2027-02-28): How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?\nLadder: rung 1 Strongly bullish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $400 billion. / rung 2 Bullish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $350 billion and less than $400 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $300 billion and less than $350 billion. / rung 4 Bearish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is at least $250 billion and less than $300 billion. / rung 5 Strongly bearish: FY2027 Data Center revenue is les\n\nRelations: v8 is part of v4. For each of FY2027 Q3, FY2027 Q4 and for the outcomes, the part's figure may not exceed the whole's: for every value of anything both rest on, and otherwise the part's low end may not exceed the whole's high end.\nScopes: NVIDIA revenue Data Center is part of NVIDIA revenue company. A sum never adds the part into the whole for the same period; a difference may take the part from the whole of the same period only to give the rest.\nShared quantities, one forecast figure each, through which every figure an outcome uses for that quantity goes: NVIDIA, revenue, company, FY2027 Q3; NVIDIA, revenue, company, FY2027 Q4.\nS/user.txt\n[Family] members:\nThesis v6 (ai-capex, theme, focus \"Combined data-center capital expenditures of the four largest AI hyperscalers\", 2026, due 2027-02-28): How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data-center capital expenditures in calendar 2026?\nLadder: rung 1 Lowest range: Combined spending is below $500 billion. / rung 2 Lower-middle range: Combined spending is at least $500 billion and below $600 billion. / rung 3 Neutral: Combined spending is at least $600 billion and below $700 billion. / rung 4 Upper-middle range: Combined spending is at least $700 billion and below $800 billion. / rung 5 Highest range: Combined spending is at least $800 billion.\n\nRelations: none.\nShared quantities, one forecast figure each, through which every figure an outcome uses for that quantity goes: none.\nOutcome keys (population | measure | scope | period), in USD bn, to be used exactly: v6 = four largest AI hyperscalers | data-center capex | combined | CY2026.\n\n[Evidence in view for the family, 50 items]\n- e122 [third_party_view; Autonocion.com; original source Tom’s Hardware ; from gnews:417f6244f0aaa27123023deb 2026-07-06] Tom’s Hardware’s running tally said more than 75 U.S. data-center projects worth around $130 billion had been blocked or delayed so far in 2026.\nE/schema.json 249:      \"description\": \"The members for which this figure is the market's reference. It and every figure beneath it is a source or a computed figure, never an estimate or a forecast, and at least one of them is a quoted consensus, guidance or outside figure. A past period's reported share or multi\n273:   \"description\": \"The family's calculation. Use one forecast figure for each quantity and period, as a point or a range, wherever that quantity is needed (outside figures beneath it, or a point a final range rests on, are fine). A growth rate computed from guidance may serve as a stated benchma\nO/schema.json 264:      \"description\": \"The members for which this figure is the market's reference. It and every figure beneat