{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba claude-r56.md; nl -ba small_cases.py | sed -n '631,660p'; nl -ba s4-ratestop-calc_small.py.txt | sed -n '626,657p'; rg -n -i 'D741|third reader|threshold|decision' ../../../../hivemind/.claude/skills/council-loop/SKILL.md | tail -n 20\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Round 56, Claude's own reflection (written before reading Codex's)\n     2\t\n     3\t## The verdict\n     4\tSTOP is correct as registered: a Part B refusal of a right answer (P-v4/Claude, S4). The other lines pass as written, including \"an\n     5\taccepted reply with a named defect (marked by both readers, or by the third reader)\". In R07 both readers marked F3, but under\n     6\tdifferent types (one marked \"own estimate as reference\", the other \"two forecasts\"). Neither type was marked by both readers, and\n     7\tneither was upheld by both adjudicators. I score the line as written: no settled defect. I also disclose that both readers flagged F3.\n     8\t\n     9\t## The mechanism (one class, one case)\n    10\tS4's bypass walk descends through every non-forecast figure, % and x included. A rate computed from a quarter's guidance supplies no\n    11\tvalue of that quarter. The census over all 24 stored v13s replies: 1 changes (this refusal), 23 unchanged; 104 of 104 cases pass on\n    12\tthe copy.\n    13\t\n    14\tThe request pulls both ways:\n    15\t- the system text says guidance gives \"a run-rate that carries the guided growth forward\";\n    16\t- the schema says a guidance growth rate \"may serve as a stated benchmark for an estimate\";\n    17\t- the header says \"Shared quantities … through which every figure an outcome uses for that quantity goes\".\n    18\tBoth refusal reviewers read the header as stating the refusal, and both judged the answer right. So the rule as written refuses a right\n    19\tanswer. The request and code should move together.\n    20\t\n    21\t## The proposed change (one lever)\n    22\t1. Code: S4's walk does not descend below a figure whose unit is % or x. A % or x figure carrying the shared key itself is still\n    23\t   reached.\n    24\t2. Request: one sentence aligned with D741 ruling 1. The schema's benchmark sentence becomes \"A growth rate computed from guidance may\n    25\t   be applied to your forecast or serve as a stated benchmark for an estimate; the quarter's value in the calculation stays your one\n    26\t   forecast figure.\" The header line becomes \"… through which every value of that quantity an outcome uses goes (a growth rate\n    27\t   computed from it is another quantity).\"\n    28\t3. Tests: an A1 case (a guidance-implied rate applied directly to the forecast passes); an A2 case (that rate applied to Q2 to rebuild\n    29\t   a Q3 value used beside the forecast is still S4); a mutant that removes the stop and must fail the A1 case.\n    30\t\n    31\tRisk I see: a writer can rebuild the guided Q3 under a non-shared label through a multiple (product(Q2, ratio(G, Q2))) and use it as\n    32\tanother quantity. That is relabelling, which S4 never caught when the label differs. The fix does not widen that hole for a USD bn\n    33\tfigure keyed as the shared quarter.\n    34\t\n    35\t## The two reader splits\n    36\t- **O's \"$18B\".** This is a source reading, and it decides O's rung. Ruling 2 settles R07's reference claim by its letter. The rest\n    37\t  (\"two forecasts\" for a part labelled as the whole; R11 supported) is a family threshold. The council-loop trap says boundary splits\n    38\t  go to Alex. My lean: report it to Alex as a disclosed ambiguity beside the request for the paid re-send, not as a blocking question.\n    39\t  The answers state the reading as their assumption, which is what D737 wanted readers to see.\n    40\t- **Prose numbers.** By the registered definitions they are not defects. They are, however, exactly \"hallucinated numbers\" in what an\n    41\t  analyst reads. This is outside D737's code scope. A fix would be a new mechanism (for example a prose-to-figure check), and it is\n    42\t  Alex's product call, not a v13s blocker. My lean: count them in the paid re-send as a secondary reader line, and tell Alex.\n    43\t\n    44\t## The next step (one recommendation)\n    45\tBuild the change with its cases and mutant, $0. Re-check all 24 stored replies and the rehearsal. Then run one fresh blind test\n    46\t(12 writers, $0), because the request bytes change and only a send shows how writers read the new sentence. If it is clean, take it to\n    47\tAlex as the request for the paid re-send, with the two disclosures.\n    48\t\n    49\tThe alternative is to go to Alex now with \"12 of 12 accepted on the same replies after the fix\". That judges a fixed checker on the\n    50\ttest that found the error, and the changed sentence would be untested.\n   631\tdef main():\n   632\t    failures = 0\n   633\t    for group, name, expect, recorded, build in CASES:\n   634\t        answer, family = build()\n   635\t        result = run(copy.deepcopy(answer), family)\n   636\t        if 'schema' in result:\n   637\t            got = 'schema'\n   638\t            detail = result['schema'][:1]\n   639\t        else:\n   640\t            codes = sorted({c for c, _ in result['errors']})\n   641\t            got = 'pass' if not codes else ','.join(codes)\n   642\t            detail = result['errors'][:2]\n   643\t        ok = got == expect                               # [54] exactly the registered rule(s): no other refusal may stand in for it\n   644\t        if ok and name in MESSAGES and not any(MESSAGES[name] in d for _, d in result.get('errors', [])):\n   645\t            ok, detail = False, [f'the refusal does not say \"{MESSAGES[name]}\"'] + list(result.get('errors', []))[:2]\n   646\t        if ok and recorded:\n   647\t            ok = any(r['type'] == recorded for r in result.get('recorded', []))\n   648\t            if not ok:\n   649\t                detail = [f'missing recorded {recorded}: {[r[\"type\"] for r in result.get(\"recorded\", [])]}']\n   650\t        failures += not ok\n   651\t        print(f'{\"PASS\" if ok else \"FAIL\"}  {group}  {name}  [expected {expect}{\" + recorded \" + recorded if recorded else \"\"}; got {got}]'\n   652\t              + ('' if ok else f'  {json.dumps(detail, ensure_ascii=False)[:400]}'))\n   653\t    print(f'{len(CASES) - failures} of {len(CASES)} cases as registered')\n   654\t    return 1 if failures else 0\n   655\t\n   656\t\n   657\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   658\t    raise SystemExit(main())\n   626\t        if len(ids) > 1:\n   627\t            errors.append(('S4', f'{\" | \".join(k)}: {len(ids)} forecasts ({\", \".join(sorted(ids))}); compute it once and use that figure'))\n   628\t    for want in family.get('shared', []):\n   629\t        key = _key(want)\n   630\t        node = by_key.get(key) or nodes.get(key, [])\n   631\t        for v, out in sorted(outcomes.items()):\n   632\t            reached, stack, seen_ids = [], [out], set()\n   633\t            while stack:\n   634\t                fid = stack.pop()\n   635\t                if fid in seen_ids or fid not in figs:\n   636\t                    continue\n   637\t                seen_ids.add(fid)\n   638\t                f = figs[fid]\n   639\t                if _key(f['what']) == key:\n   640\t                    reached.append(fid)\n   641\t                    if f['basis'] == 'forecast':\n   642\t                        continue                           # through the forecast figure: what lies beneath it is its basis\n   643\t                if f['unit'] in ('%', 'x'):\n   644\t                    continue                               # a rate or multiple is another quantity: what it is computed from supplies no value of this one\n   645\t                stack.extend(f.get('inputs') or [])\n   646\t            if not reached:\n   647\t                continue\n   648\t            if len(node) != 1:\n   649\t                errors.append(('S4', f'{v}: uses {\" | \".join(key)} but the calculation has {len(node)} forecast figures for it'))\n   650\t                continue\n   651\t            bypass = sorted(r for r in reached if r != node[0])      # the walk never descends below the forecast figure\n   652\t            if bypass:\n   653\t                errors.append(('S4', f'{v}: uses {\", \".join(bypass)} for {\" | \".join(key)} beside its forecast figure {node[0]}'))\n   654\t    return errors\n   655\t\n   656\t\n   657\tdef _part_whole(family, figs, calc, outcomes):\n3:description: Drive a measured improvement of one pipeline step to a pass line Alex sets, in rounds, with a Codex–Claude council at every decision. Use it when a step's quality must be raised or a new step validated. It takes the work from census to mechanism, independent council, cheap probe, blind scoring, council on the results, whole-bench run, a source-backed pass-line verdict, a written log, and a reflection council for the next angle. Alex, 2026-11-07 - \"我觉得这几次的循环很有效的逼近问题我觉得应该把他写成一个skill\".\n44:- Search the decisions and earlier experiment logs for the mechanism by name (AGENTS §2.4); quote what they rejected.\n63:  - a required field that forces the decision per item (closest open thesis, why a separate bet);\n70:- **Each arm states its source:** a line of the standard, a decision, or Alex's words. It states its falsifier before it is sent.\n153:  a forward simulation, detection was close. Score the decision the product takes per record on the library it would really see; a\n163:- **Model readers carry their family's threshold.** Two adjudicators given the same rubric sided with their own families (17 of 52\n184:  must_not. When the two references split widely, that is Alex's decision.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22 && jq -r '.[]|[.case,.writer,.stage,.decision, (.published|to_entries|map(.key+\\\"=\\\"+(.value[0]|tostring))|join(\\\"/\\\"))]|@tsv' CHECKED.json; for f in */answers/*.json; do printf '%s ' \\\"\"'$f\"; jq -c '\"'{outcomes:[.figures[]|select((.outcome_for|length)>0)|[.id,.value,.low,.high,.inputs]],answers:[.answers[]|[.view_id,.rung]]}' \\\"\"'$f\"; done; for w in claude codex; do jq -r '\"'.figures[]|select(.kind==\\\"source\\\")|[.id,.quote_number,.evidence_id]|@tsv' E/answers/\"'$w.json; done; rg -n -C 1 '\"'from \\\\\"'$35 billion to '\"\\\\\"'$170 billion'\"' E/user.txt\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_31","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22 && jq -r '.[]|[.case,.writer,.stage,.decision, (.published|to_entries|map(.key+\\\"=\\\"+(.value[0]|tostring))|join(\\\"/\\\"))]|@tsv' CHECKED.json; for f in */answers/*.json; do printf '%s ' \\\"\"'$f\"; jq -c '\"'{outcomes:[.figures[]|select((.outcome_for|length)>0)|[.id,.value,.low,.high,.inputs]],answers:[.answers[]|[.view_id,.rung]]}' \\\"\"'$f\"; done; for w in claude codex; do jq -r '\"'.figures[]|select(.kind==\\\"source\\\")|[.id,.quote_number,.evidence_id]|@tsv' E/answers/\"'$w.json; done; rg -n -C 1 '\"'from \\\\\"'$35 billion to '\"\\\\\"'$170 billion'\"' E/user.txt\"","aggregated_output":"P\tclaude\tchecked\tpublish\tv4=413.14/v8=382.39164\nP\tcodex\tchecked\tpublish\tv4=419.21999999999997/v8=388.32032\nP-v4\tclaude\tchecked\trefused\tv4=416.6193762993763\nP-v4\tcodex\tchecked\tpublish\tv4=416.40000000000003\nP-v8\tclaude\tchecked\tpublish\tv8=383.56728000000004\nP-v8\tcodex\tchecked\tpublish\tv8=388.56999999999994\nS\tclaude\tchecked\tpublish\tv6=717.8\nS\tcodex\tchecked\tpublish\tv6=680.8\nO\tclaude\tchecked\tpublish\tv29=14.0\nO\tcodex\tchecked\tpublish\tv29=16.0\nE\tclaude\tchecked\tpublish\tv41=36.0\nE\tcodex\tchecked\tpublish\tv41=36.0\nE/answers/claude.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F10\",36,null,null,[\"F3\",\"F9\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v41\",3]]}\nE/answers/codex.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F6\",36,null,null,[\"F3\",\"F5\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v41\",3]]}\nO/answers/claude.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F10\",14,null,null,[\"F3\",\"F9\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v29\",1]]}\nO/answers/codex.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F10\",16,null,null,[\"F3\",\"F9\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v29\",1]]}\nP-v4/answers/claude.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F11\",416.62,null,null,[\"F3\",\"F8\",\"F10\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v4\",2]]}\nP-v4/answers/codex.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F12\",416.4,null,null,[\"F1\",\"F2\",\"F6\",\"F11\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v4\",2]]}\nP-v8/answers/claude.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F17\",383.56,null,null,[\"F1\",\"F2\",\"F15\",\"F16\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v8\",2]]}\nP-v8/answers/codex.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F17\",388.57,null,null,[\"F4\",\"F12\",\"F16\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v8\",2]]}\nP/answers/claude.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F9\",413.14,null,null,[\"F3\",\"F8\"]],[\"F16\",382.39,null,null,[\"F13\",\"F15\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v4\",2],[\"v8\",2]]}\nP/answers/codex.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F9\",419.22,null,null,[\"F1\",\"F2\",\"F6\",\"F8\"]],[\"F20\",388.32032,null,null,[\"F11\",\"F12\",\"F18\",\"F19\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v4\",2],[\"v8\",2]]}\nS/answers/claude.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F11\",717.8,null,null,[\"F9\",\"F10\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v6\",4]]}\nS/answers/codex.json {\"outcomes\":[[\"F8\",680.8,null,null,[\"F6\",\"F7\"]]],\"answers\":[[\"v6\",3]]}\nF1\t$20 billion\te3660\nF2\tdouble\te3660\nF4\t$35 billion\te4857\nF5\t$170 billion\te4857\nF6\t50%\te4687\nF1\t$20 billion\te3660\nF2\tdouble\te4856\nF4\t20%\te5399\n30-- e4857 [third_party_view; fool.com (analyst); original source Bank of America analysts ; from gnews:c70bc12967b9b53426b5fb10 2026-09-12] Bank of America analysts forecast that the CPU market would grow fivefold, from $35 billion in 2026 to $170 billion in 2030.\n31:    Quote: Analysts at Bank of America also released a research report in June, saying they believe the CPU market will grow fivefold between this year and 2030, from $35 billion to $170 billion.\n32-    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e935; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '319,372p'; rg -n '\"'^## D439|''^## D509'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n --hidden -g '\"'!**/*.stream'\"' 'calibration-D741' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_32","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba AGENTS.md | sed -n '319,372p'; rg -n '\"'^## D439|''^## D509'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; rg -n --hidden -g '\"'!**/*.stream'\"' 'calibration-D741' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"   319\t- Pair every structural check with its semantic one. Run a data rule over its whole input range and on cases it was not tuned on. Weigh\n   320\t  a case by what it carries in the product, not by count.\n   321\t- A claim about a population (\"the data is clean\") rests on a code sweep of the whole population and an independent read of a fresh\n   322\t  random sample, never on the pages the author looked at.\n   323\t- Cost is priced from tokens at the published rates (`hivemind.model.PRICES`, cached input at `model.CACHED_INPUT_SHARE`), never from a\n   324\t  stored `cost_usd`; say which rates a projection uses.\n   325\t\n   326\t### 7.3 Iterating\n   327\t\n   328\t- **One class at a time** (Alex, 2026-10-29: \"你一类一类改，快速迭代然后测regression\"). Count the misses by mechanism; take the largest\n   329\t  class; trace it to the sentence that causes it; change one thing aimed at that class; run the whole bench (a prompt change alters every\n   330\t  request) against the previous version; read every regression to its raw answer. The pages that showed the failure locate its\n   331\t  mechanism; only the whole bench (every set, every draw) accepts the change.\n   332\t- **Name the effect on the judgement first.** Every proposed change states the effect it is expected to have on a reader or on the final\n   333\t  judgement, and is tested there where possible; a step's own counts do not decide it alone. A fix that keeps moving its error to\n   334\t  neighbouring cases stops being tuned on that set (Alex, 2026-11-09: \"感觉现在一直在修一些mknor的原地打转，你是不是要思考下现在具体还差什么high priority big impact 的需要做？\";\n   335\t  he approved this rule the same day, D391).\n   336\t- **A model call is a sampler.** Re-send a stored request before calling its answer a defect. Totals and acceptance come from at least\n   337\t  three samples beside a fresh control; a bar the control fails against itself judges nothing. A direct-read pass\n   338\t  (one send per article, every answer read beside its source; D238) locates mechanisms; its counts are one draw and are labelled so.\n   339\t- **A written log.** One row per arm: hypothesis, change, numbers against the control (regressions first), kept or not. Refuted arms and\n   340\t  your own mistakes stay in it; the next session starts from its last row.\n   341\t- **Own the loop, within what Alex agreed.** When the direction is agreed and no stop is in force (`CURRENT_STATE.md`), push your own\n   342\t  hypotheses through $0 checks and probes of a few cents on stored cases without asking. A registered test, an end-to-end run, or\n   343\t  anything that departs from the agreed plan starts on his word; a result that contradicts the hypothesis stops the line and goes to him\n   344\t  (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\"). While he is not active (D439), \"his word\" is the council's\n   345\t  recorded consensus, and a stopped line goes to the council for re-assessment.\n   346\t- **Council before every change is sent.** A prompt, schema, code or criterion change, including one found by reading a probe, is a new\n   347\t  arm. It goes to an independent Codex read and a challenge round before its first send, and its result goes to a challenge round\n   348\t  before the next change. Reading the traces and the model's own account locates a fix; it does not review it (Alex, 2026-11-08:\n   349\t  \"你这些改动有我你有好好的跑council 再下手\").\n   350\t  Every round's reasoning and decisions are reflected on in the council until there is a consensus; the decision is recorded, and\n   351\t  the next test goes straight ahead, held to the PRD and its quantified goals, with every trace read by you yourself and not only\n   352\t  by readers (Alex, 2026-11-10: \"你应该跑council loop 来reflect 你每一轮的思路还有决策，需要你打成共识，记录决策，向前直行测试。不要drift,我们有PRD和量化目标，\n   353\t  你自己作为llm 下去看所有trace\").\n   354\t- **Small first, then one run.** A hypothesis is first validated the simplest way, on a few stored cases and a few cents, and shown to\n   355\t  work at a high level before any full analysis or stability test is built (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"don't overspend resources on wasting time.\n   356\t  We need to validate the hypothesis in a very simple way and to make sure that it works on a high level before we dive into do the full\n   357\t  analysis stability test. This is a principle you should remember\"). A day or week slice before any whole-corpus run; preflight on\n   358\t  stored data before any paid run (§5); no edit while a run is live (§9). A paid run measures a configuration; it never tries a fix.\n   359\t  Before each send, write what it can still change in the decision and which risk the cheaper check left uncovered; a replicate or\n   360\t  control that only re-measures noise or a settled comparison is not sent, and a fix is not sent before the model's own account and the\n   361\t  request locate where the decision is made (Alex, 2026-10-30: \"你跑这么多次真的有意义吗\"; \"我感觉你在为了跑而跑\"). Several fixes on one\n   362\t  base are each proved on stored data in minutes and then run together once (Alex, 2026-11-02: \"快速验证。不要drift,不要跑超级繁琐的全方位验证，先poc 改，能work,有结论，全部改动放到一起再跑完整\"; D266).\n   363\t- **One recommendation, one test.** What reaches Alex as the next step of work is one recommendation and one test of it, reached after\n   364\t  rounds of review (Claude's own, Codex's, an independent reader's) on the traces until a round finds nothing serious; never a menu of\n   365\t  arms or options, never a conclusion the next probe overturns (a choice that changes what the system does still goes to him with its\n   366\t  options and a recommendation, Authority and scope) (Alex, 2026-11-04: \"就测试一种，一次 … 你就没有自己看5轮review，能不能自己有个超级自信的定论和证据再给我提建议？\").\n   367\t  An agreed recommendation is first challenged by an independent reader on the concrete evidence behind it (\"why you give\n   368\t  recommendations for this. What did you see exactly?\"). A review round reads a rule as its author meant it; only a send shows how the\n   369\t  model applies it: before a registered test, the changed request is sent on the cases that motivated it, a few cents.\n   370\t- **A failed arm is diagnosed before the next one.** When an arm fixes its class and regresses another, write the root cause first: the\n   371\t  process error (what grew, what the small sample did not guard) and the mechanism, traced to the raw answers and the model's account,\n   372\t  never a guess stated as the cause. A small sample guards every class the change can move, not only its own. When a fix keeps moving\n4871:## D439 · 2026-11-13 · While Alex is not active, the council decides by consensus and the loop iterates to the PRD's production goals\n5902:## D509 · 2026-11-15 · Alex goes inactive: Claude operates by his rules, and every round's run is examined in depth with the council (D439 in force again)\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md:460:- **The reader calibration on six stored boundary replies** (`calibration-D741/`) runs before the re-run.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22 && rg -n '\\\"packet\\\"|\\\"decision\\\"|\\\"codex\\\"|\\\"claude\\\"' TALLY.json | tail -n 42; nl -ba adjudication/R11.codex.json | sed -n '1,51p'; nl -ba adjudication/R09.codex.json | sed -n '1,50p'; nl -ba adjudication/R03.claude.json | sed -n '1,42p'; nl -ba BUILD.txt; nl -ba E/answers/codex.json | sed -n '1,100p'; rg -n 's4_census' /Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd poc/data/judging-v13s-blind2-2026-11-22 && rg -n '\\\"packet\\\"|\\\"decision\\\"|\\\"codex\\\"|\\\"claude\\\"' TALLY.json | tail -n 42; nl -ba adjudication/R11.codex.json | sed -n '1,51p'; nl -ba adjudication/R09.codex.json | sed -n '1,50p'; nl -ba adjudication/R03.claude.json | sed -n '1,42p'; nl -ba BUILD.txt; nl -ba E/answers/codex.json | sed -n '1,100p'; rg -n 's4_census' /Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND2-RESULT.md\"","aggregated_output":"291:    \"claude\": []\n295:   \"packet\": \"R10\",\n297:   \"writer\": \"codex\",\n298:   \"decision\": \"publish\",\n315:     \"codex\": \"reject\",\n316:     \"claude\": \"reject\"\n320:    \"codex\": [\n328:    \"claude\": []\n332:   \"packet\": \"R11\",\n334:   \"writer\": \"claude\",\n335:   \"decision\": \"publish\",\n354:     \"codex\": \"uphold\",\n355:     \"claude\": \"reject\"\n363:     \"codex\": \"reject\",\n364:     \"claude\": \"reject\"\n374:     \"codex\": \"reject\",\n375:     \"claude\": \"reject\"\n383:     \"codex\": \"uphold\",\n384:     \"claude\": \"reject\"\n395:     \"codex\": \"uphold\",\n396:     \"claude\": \"reject\"\n400:    \"codex\": [\n439:    \"claude\": []\n443:   \"packet\": \"R12\",\n445:   \"writer\": \"claude\",\n446:   \"decision\": \"publish\",\n455:    \"codex\": [],\n456:    \"claude\": []\n466:    \"codex\",\n476:    \"claude\",\n486:    \"codex\",\n496:    \"claude\",\n506:    \"claude\",\n520:    \"claude\",\n530:    \"claude\",\n540:    \"codex\",\n552:    \"codex\",\n565:    \"claude\",\n575:    \"claude\",\n585:    \"claude\",\n599:    \"claude\",\n611:    \"claude\",\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"members\": {\n     3\t    \"v29\": {\n     4\t      \"supported\": \"no\",\n     5\t      \"why\": \"The $14 billion forecast falls in rung 1, but its calculation depends on subtracting $18 billion from the July balance by fiscal year-end. e2889 says NVIDIA had '$18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year.' The answer states its assumption that the $18 billion belongs to the July balance, but presents year-end funding as company guidance. The passage gives no payment schedule. If the full $18 billion slips, the July balance alone remains $25 billion, the lower edge of rung 2.\"\n     6\t    }\n     7\t  },\n     8\t  \"defects\": [\n     9\t    {\n    10\t      \"reader\": \"Reader 1\",\n    11\t      \"type\": \"number misread\",\n    12\t      \"figures\": [\"F2\", \"F3\", \"F10\"],\n    13\t      \"decision\": \"uphold\",\n    14\t      \"why\": \"e2889 says NVIDIA 'has $18 billion committed to equity investments for the rest of its fiscal year.' F2 turns the amount committed into guidance for funding existing commitments in Q3–Q4. That change supplies the unsupported deduction used in F3 and F10.\"\n    15\t    },\n    16\t    {\n    17\t      \"reader\": \"Reader 1\",\n    18\t      \"type\": \"number misread\",\n    19\t      \"figures\": [\"F4\"],\n    20\t      \"decision\": \"reject\",\n    21\t      \"why\": \"The quote says 'up to $3 billion' for the deal and 'an additional $1 billion based on the company meeting' conditions for the second tranche. The format asks for 'the qualifier the quote writes just before the number.' The quoted $1 billion has no 'up to' immediately before it, and F4 identifies the tranche as milestone-based.\"\n    22\t    },\n    23\t    {\n    24\t      \"reader\": \"Reader 1\",\n    25\t      \"type\": \"wrong arithmetic\",\n    26\t      \"figures\": [\"F11\", \"F1\", \"F12\"],\n    27\t      \"decision\": \"reject\",\n    28\t      \"why\": \"The format says 'The value is the number as written' and defines 'sum(a, b, …) = a + b + …'. F11 records 42 as its value and 'more than' separately as its qualifier. The stored values sum to 67. In financial terms, the qualifier makes $67 billion a lower bound on the total.\"\n    29\t    },\n    30\t    {\n    31\t      \"reader\": \"Reader 1\",\n    32\t      \"type\": \"number misread\",\n    33\t      \"figures\": [\"F13\"],\n    34\t      \"decision\": \"uphold\",\n    35\t      \"why\": \"e1732 says NVIDIA 'has committed to directly providing $70 billion in equity investments into ecosystem partners.' It gives neither a measurement period nor a breakdown of funded and unfunded investments. F13 adds both qualifications to the cited amount. Its proximity to F12 does not establish them.\"\n    36\t    },\n    37\t    {\n    38\t      \"reader\": \"Reader 1\",\n    39\t      \"type\": \"wrong arithmetic\",\n    40\t      \"figures\": [\"F1\", \"F2\", \"F3\", \"F10\"],\n    41\t      \"decision\": \"uphold\",\n    42\t      \"why\": \"The answer says that if 'the $18B funding slips into FY2028,' the balance would 'probably keep it below $25B.' In that scenario, the deduction falls to zero and the opening $25 billion remains outstanding before any additions. Rung 1 requires a balance 'below $25 billion.'\"\n    43\t    }\n    44\t  ]\n    45\t}     1\t{\n     2\t  \"members\": {\n     3\t    \"v4\": {\n     4\t      \"supported\": \"yes\",\n     5\t      \"why\": \"Reported Q1 and Q2 revenue sum to $177.82 billion (e111, e2649). The $111 billion Q3 estimate reflects recent guidance beats and the evidence of tight supply (e2720, e3200, e2452, e5054, e5055, e3733, e4911). Carrying the 12% sequential growth benchmark into Q4 as an assumption gives $124.32 billion for Q4 and $413.14 billion for FY2027, within rung 2.\"\n     6\t    },\n     7\t    \"v8\": {\n     8\t      \"supported\": \"yes\",\n     9\t      \"why\": \"Reported Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue sum to $164.25 billion (e109, e2650). The rise in Data Center's share to 92.5% and the expected growth from Vera Rubin, ACIE, and hyperscalers support the assumed 92.7% H2 share (e3399, e2721, e5061, e3406). Applying that share to $235.32 billion gives $218.14 billion for H2 and $382.39 billion for FY2027, within rung 2 and below total company revenue.\"\n    10\t    }\n    11\t  },\n    12\t  \"defects\": [\n    13\t    {\n    14\t      \"reader\": \"Reader 1\",\n    15\t      \"type\": \"number misread\",\n    16\t      \"figures\": [\"F4\"],\n    17\t      \"decision\": \"reject\",\n    18\t      \"why\": \"F4 copies e2720's complete expression, \\\"$108 billion, plus or minus 2%.\\\" The format rule permits a plus-or-minus expression to be \\\"given as low and high or its midpoint as value.\\\" F4 uses the permitted $108 billion midpoint.\"\n    19\t    },\n    20\t    {\n    21\t      \"reader\": \"Reader 1\",\n    22\t      \"type\": \"wrong arithmetic\",\n    23\t      \"figures\": [],\n    24\t      \"decision\": \"uphold\",\n    25\t      \"why\": \"The example \\\"$115bn, then 20% sequential growth\\\" gives $138 billion in Q4 and $253 billion in H2. Adding $177.82 billion for H1 gives $430.82 billion, below rung 1's requirement of \\\"at least $431.2 billion.\\\"\"\n    26\t    },\n    27\t    {\n    28\t      \"reader\": \"Reader 1\",\n    29\t      \"type\": \"number misread\",\n    30\t      \"figures\": [],\n    31\t      \"decision\": \"uphold\",\n    32\t      \"why\": \"The explanation calls both agreements \\\"6 GW\\\" deals. e1040 says OpenAI selected AMD \\\"to deploy 6 gigawatts of GPUs,\\\" while e1041 says Meta \\\"signed for up to 6 gigawatts of Instinct GPUs.\\\" The explanation drops Meta's upper-limit qualifier.\"\n    33\t    }\n    34\t  ]\n    35\t}     1\t{\n     2\t \"members\": {\n     3\t  \"v4\": {\n     4\t   \"supported\": \"yes\",\n     5\t   \"why\": \"H1 177.82 (e111, e2649; matches e4992); F8 112.5 stated estimate (e2652 midpoint plus about 4% beat from e3200, e2452, e5056; cut back by e3733, e4911); F10 = 112.5 x 1.1227 = 126.3, 12.27% = 108.0/96.2 - 1, carrying the rate forward a stated assumption (e3406, e4283); total 416.62, rung 2; reference $411bn consensus (e4333); 70% items read as FY2028 (e5227, e2691).\"\n     6\t  }\n     7\t },\n     8\t \"defects\": [\n     9\t  {\n    10\t   \"reader\": \"Reader 1\",\n    11\t   \"type\": \"number misread\",\n    12\t   \"figures\": [],\n    13\t   \"decision\": \"reject\",\n    14\t   \"why\": \"Type covers 'a source figure's number, scale, sign or qualifier'; no figure carries the Vera Rubin 20%, prose only; number and qualifier match ('about 20%'); 'already' overstates e2721's expectation: a wording flaw in prose, enters no figure.\"\n    15\t  },\n    16\t  {\n    17\t   \"reader\": \"Reader 1\",\n    18\t   \"type\": \"wrong arithmetic\",\n    19\t   \"figures\": [],\n    20\t   \"decision\": \"reject\",\n    21\t   \"why\": \"Type covers a computed figure not equal to its operation; no computed figure carries the Morningstar comparison; 'flat' has a supported reading (H2 197 with Q3 DC about 99.9 at the midpoint, e3401, leaves Q4 about 97); all computed figures recompute within 0.5%.\"\n    22\t  }\n    23\t ],\n    24\t \"_note\": \"Condensed by Claude from the Claude adjudicator hand-back (decisions and figures verbatim; reasons shortened).\"\n    25\t}     1\tP     joint         members ['v4', 'v8'] passages 296 (79 quotes absent from the gate) request 171447 chars\n     2\tP-v4  separate-v4   members ['v4'] passages 296 (79 quotes absent from the gate) request 170525 chars\n     3\tP-v8  separate-v8   members ['v8'] passages 296 (79 quotes absent from the gate) request 170633 chars\n     4\tS     single        members ['v6'] passages 50 (41 quotes absent from the gate) request 40044 chars\n     5\tO     single        members ['v29'] passages 30 (0 quotes absent from the gate) request 35489 chars\n     6\tE     single        members ['v41'] passages 15 (0 quotes absent from the gate) request 26590 chars\n     1\t{\n     2\t  \"figures\": [\n     3\t    {\n     4\t      \"id\": \"F1\",\n     5\t      \"what\": {\n     6\t        \"population\": \"NVIDIA\",\n     7\t        \"measure\": \"revenue\",\n     8\t        \"scope\"